    "turn_text": "One thing that stands out to me about September 10 in the days and weeks preceding the 11th is This was a period that environmentalists had been waiting for and advocating for where the attention of the Congress and the country could be finally placed on this emerging crisis. And of course, all of that changed the following day. It was a very different place in the months leading up to September 11th, a very different set of national priorities, very different mood in the country, a different sense of our own security. You know, as always, very secure in our homeland. And the last thing any of us could imagine would be a major attack on American soil. We've been the subject of different terrorist attacks and plots in the past, but nothing like we would experience. And it would propel the country in a very different direction.",
