    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "All those points being taken, we've spoken to other people who have thought very deeply about this topic and heard the sort of same refrain, which is there was an assumption after 9-11 that it would change everything. And we did see this moment of unity, of kind of a rallying together. And then we didn't. And then American politics, if anything, has become more polarized even than it was in the lead-up to 9-11, where you had a very fractious presidential election in 2000. And some people say it's better to think of 9-11 and its impact is perhaps more of an interlude than a fundamental change. I'm wondering what you think of that.",
