  {
    "episode_id": 48681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think 9-11 will bring about some fundamental changes, most particularly in recognition of the limits of military power. in terms of whether 9-11 was, could have been expected to be a transformational event in terms of national unity and cohesion. Even then, I would not have expected that to be a unending phenomenon, just given what we've seen of the country's history and what we know of human nature. Even an event as dramatic as that isn't going to change things indelibly. So I'm not surprised that the unifying impact of that tragedy has dissipated over time. It's probably more a question of what we should have expected for how long it would have lasted than whether it meant expectations or not.",
